## Secrets (API keys, tokens)

- Never ask me to paste a key into this chat, a file or the terminal.
- When you need a new key, ask me to "Drop Key it as `<name>`" (use a short kebab-case name, e.g. `openai-api`). I'll save it with the Drop Key app. Then check it's there with `dropkey has <name>`.
- Read keys only inside the command that uses them, e.g.
  `OPENAI_API_KEY="$(dropkey get openai-api)" python3 script.py`
  or pipe them straight into the tool that stores them.
- Never print a key's value, never echo it, never write it into a file in this project, and never put it in a commit.
- To see which keys exist, run `dropkey list`. It shows names only.
